-- title:
--   The packed block-$0$ gate table flattens to the $2602$ low slots
-- statement:
--   # Flattening the packed block-0 gate table
--
--   The $1301$ block-0 mix-forward gates are stored as $6$-tuples
--   $$
--   (n,\ \mathrm{piv},\ \mathrm{bp},\ n_{\mathrm{fresh}},\ t_{\mathrm{piv}},\ t_{\mathrm{bp}}).
--   $$
--   The associated low-slot list is the concatenation, in pack order, of $\mathrm{piv}$ and $\mathrm{bp}-1$ for each tuple. This definition records that flattened list and proves it equals the explicit $2602$-element list used by the companion Nodup certificate, by comparing the two sides on fifty-gate chunks and gluing the identities along concatenation.
--
--   Together with that Nodup certificate, the low slots of the packed table are pairwise distinct. The pack is a prefix table only; it does not identify the later mix-forward blocks or the full word $W_{1F}$.
-- source:
--   IntMul Kappa R8 Bit Oppbank FormalOK: equality of gateLowsOf(gatePack) with the 2602-element lows list, for the 1301 packed block-0 mix-forward gates on QHNetRecR (97df824b). Helper pack for the prefix lemma MovesV_preF_copyoND_block0. Not a full-word W1F certificate.

/-!
Slim helper: gateLowsOf gatePack = lowsFlat, by 50-gate `rfl` chunks.
Standalone; no QHNet / Mathlib. Completes (gateLowsOf gatePack).Nodup when
combined with lowsFlat_nodup from gateLows_nodup_slim.lean.
-/
set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 8000000
set_option autoImplicit false


namespace IntMul.Kappa.R8.Bit.Oppbank.Block0LowsOf

def gatePiv (g : Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat) : Nat := g.2.1
def gateBp (g : Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat) : Nat := g.2.2.1
def gateLowsOf (gs : List (Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat × Nat)) : List Nat :=
  gs.flatMap (fun g => [gatePiv g, gateBp g - 1])


